    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid that's not really feasible, because the cleanest solution requires creating a `m` / `r` / etc. Operator-pending mappings. The hacky solution is [present in 'mini.surround' for \"add\" action](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e554890210cd29d017d6a0c1b1a46f995dcf9e64/lua/mini/surround.lua#L1259-L1264) and I'd really like to not reuse it, as it looks like relying too much on Neovim's/Vim's internals.\r\n\r\nThe built-in operators working like that is a special case (`:h operator-doubled`) due to how they are implemented internallt and I don't think can/should be replicated in custom mappings.\r\n\r\nAs there is a perfectly working alternative by using `_` textobject, I'd rather suggest sticking to it. Another reason to not remap `_` :)",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid that's not really feasible, because the cleanest solution requires creating a <code class=\"notranslate\">m</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">r</code> / etc. Operator-pending mappings. The hacky solution is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e554890210cd29d017d6a0c1b1a46f995dcf9e64/lua/mini/surround.lua#L1259-L1264\">present in 'mini.surround' for \"add\" action</a> and I'd really like to not reuse it, as it looks like relying too much on Neovim's/Vim's internals.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The built-in operators working like that is a special case (<code class=\"notranslate\">:h operator-doubled</code>) due to how they are implemented internallt and I don't think can/should be replicated in custom mappings.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As there is a perfectly working alternative by using <code class=\"notranslate\">_</code> textobject, I'd rather suggest sticking to it. Another reason to not remap <code class=\"notranslate\">_</code> :)</p>",
            "bodyText": "I am afraid that's not really feasible, because the cleanest solution requires creating a m / r / etc. Operator-pending mappings. The hacky solution is present in 'mini.surround' for \"add\" action and I'd really like to not reuse it, as it looks like relying too much on Neovim's/Vim's internals.\nThe built-in operators working like that is a special case (:h operator-doubled) due to how they are implemented internallt and I don't think can/should be replicated in custom mappings.\nAs there is a perfectly working alternative by using _ textobject, I'd rather suggest sticking to it. Another reason to not remap _ :)",
